      "writtenOn": "2024-12-26T18:26:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have to calculate power for each channel separately if we intend just to return the combined power for all channels. This is because energy and power calculation is sample-based and does not depend on the values of previous samples (see the implementation here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/media/audio_utils/include/audio_utils/power.h;l\u003d45;drc\u003d6386d8fa0d25d78b9239baa221f64cca84e8f36c). In other words, it\u0027s a linear operation. Thus, running `audio_utils_compute_power_mono` over an interleaved stereo input will produce the same result as running for each channel and then summing the result.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "1f394269b5ceb88ca6538066f07b4957195092c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
